## SQ-CWG-01 | Creative Worldgen mixins apply once, More Mooblooms and Baby Mobs nested once
@group A
@commands Boot 2: `grep -E "creativeworldgen.mixins.json\|creativeengineering.mixins.json" logs/latest.log`; `grep -c "from creativeworldgen.mixins.json" logs/debug.log`; mod list
@pass No mixin apply error; the 60 common mixins apply (minus gated ones whose mod is absent: AE2, Quark, MCA, LC, Cloud Storage, Forgiving Void, Bushier Flowers); no worldgen mixin from patcherMod (double apply); one `moremooblooms` and one `babymobs`, nested
@fails Gate id wrong in `WorldgenMixinPlugin`, a moved mixin still in patcherMod's json, or the old standalone jar left in `mods/`
@from batches/r1103/sA_2.qb
bootreject (Mixin apply failed|InvalidMixinException|MixinApplyError).*(creativeworldgen|creativeengineering)
bootreject DuplicateModsFound|Found duplicate mods
shell grep -E "creativeworldgen.mixins.json|creativeengineering.mixins.json" logs/latest.log | head -20
shell echo "mixing lines from creativeworldgen.mixins.json: $(grep -c 'from creativeworldgen.mixins.json' logs/debug.log || true)"
shell echo "worldgen mixins still applied from patcherMod json (should be none of the moved ones):"; grep -oE "Mixing [A-Za-z_.]+ from creativeengineering.mixins.json" logs/debug.log | grep -iE "worldgen|structure|locate|leaf|raid|named|forgiving|mobcap|spawn" | sort -u | head -20 || true
shell grep -oiE "(moreMooblooms|babyMobs)-[0-9.]+[^ ]*\.jar" logs/debug.log | sort | uniq -c
shell ! ls mods | grep -iE "^(moreMooblooms|babyMobs)"
look mixing count = 60 minus the gated ones whose mod is absent (AE2, Quark, MCA, LC, Cloud Storage, Forgiving Void, Bushier Flowers: those mods are installed, so expect about 60); no moved worldgen mixin from creativeengineering.mixins.json; each of moreMooblooms / babyMobs found once, from jarjar of creativeworldgen

## SQ-CWG-02 | config sections carried from creativeengineering-common.toml into creativeworldgen-common.toml (first boot)
@group A
@commands Same boot: read `config/creativeworldgen-common.toml`, `config/creativeengineering-common.toml`; restart, read again
@pass `[swaps] config sections [...] carried over`; the Worldgen file holds the edited value; `[perf]` there has only the 13 mob cap keys; after the boot the CE file has no `[worldgen]`, `[forgiving_void]`, `[leaf_decay]`, `[raids]`, `[named_mobs]` or mob cap keys; no WARN on the second boot
@fails `carrySections` ran after the config was registered
@from batches/r1103/sA_2.qb
bootexpect config sections .*carried over
shell grep -nE "config sections .*carried" logs/latest.log | head -5
shell ls -l config/creativeworldgen-common.toml && grep -nE "^\[" config/creativeworldgen-common.toml | head -40
shell awk '/^\[named_mobs\]/{s=1;next} /^\[/{s=0} s && /chance/' config/creativeworldgen-common.toml | grep -E "chance = 0\.02"
shell awk '/^\[perf\]/{s=1;next} /^\[/{s=0} s && /=/' config/creativeworldgen-common.toml | grep -vE "^\s*#" | wc -l
shell ! grep -nE "^\[(worldgen|forgiving_void|leaf_decay|raids|named_mobs)\]" config/creativeengineering-common.toml
shell grep -nE "(WARN|ERROR).*(creativeworldgen-common|creativeengineering-common)" logs/latest.log | head -5 || true
look named_mobs chance 0.02 carried (edited before this boot); [perf] in the Worldgen file has the 13 mob cap keys only (count above); the CE file lost the six sections. Second-boot half: SQ-CWG-02b in sA_3.qb

## SQ-CWG-03 | Creative Worldgen script pack loads, no missing-name errors, reports rewritten
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep -E "startup script packs in order\|creativeworldgen\|NCH.cfg\|loot-tuning" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log \| head -30`
@pass Pack `creativeworldgen` loads; no `global.CWG missing`, no `no ... section in any registered config`, no `[loot-tuning] could not read`; structure, bee nest, wild flower, mushroom and mob spawn reports rewritten
@fails `cwg_core.js` not in the jar, `registerConfig` class name, or a moved script reading a pack-scope name
@from batches/r1103/sA_2.qb
shell grep -hE "startup script packs in order" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/latest.log | head -3
shell grep -hE "startup script packs in order" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/latest.log | grep -q creativeworldgen
shell ! grep -hE "global\.CWG missing|section in any registered config|\[loot-tuning\] could not read" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log logs/latest.log
shell grep -hE "creativeworldgen|NCH\.cfg|loot-tuning" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | head -30
shell find kubejs -path kubejs/exported -prune -o -type f -newer eula.txt -print | grep -vE "\.log$" | head -30
look reports written this boot (structure, bee nest, wild flower, mushroom, mob spawn) appear in the find list

## SQ-CWG-04 | loot tuning lists the Creative Delight crate rules
@group A
@commands Same boot: `/loottuning` (or its list subcommand); `grep -iE "lootRules\|crate" logs/kubejs/server.log \| head`
@pass The CD rules (veggie, vintage, rustic, cave carrot crates) are listed, as on boot 1
@fails CD `loot.js` ran before `05_tuning.js` and its queued rules never ran
@from batches/r1103/sA_2.qb
> loottuning
sleep 2
> zloot packs crate
waitlog \[zloot\] (packs|pack[s]?) crate: \d+ 30
expect Loot tuning: active
expect \[zloot\] pack .*crate
shell grep -hiE "lootRules|crate" logs/kubejs/server.log | head -15
look veggie, vintage, rustic and cave carrot crate pairs listed (the CD rules ran after 05_tuning.js); same rule count as /loottuning on SQ-CWG-05 (sA_3.qb)
reject (Unknown (item|block|block type|entity)|Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command|\[zloot\] error)

