## SQ-CWG-07 | no wild-crops-off warning; earth fill, ground match, soils and bubble-column tags filled
@group A
@commands Same world: `grep -E "wild crops off\|biomeRules" logs/kubejs/server.log`; `/dumptags` for `#creativeengineering:earth_fill/*`, `ground_match/*`, `worldgen/grass_like_soils`, entity `bubble_column_immune`
@pass No "wild crops off" warning (CD reads `global.biomeRules` at event time); every tag filled
@fails Tag rows lost in the `blocktags.js` split, or the CD guard tripping
@from batches/r1103/sA_4.qb
shell ! grep -hE "wild crops off" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/latest.log
shell grep -hE "biomeRules" logs/kubejs/server.log | head -5 || true
> dumptags
waitlog (Dumped|dumptags|tags/) 300
sleep 10
shell python3 -c "import json;b=json.load(open('kubejs/exported/tags/block_tags.json'));e=json.load(open('kubejs/exported/tags/entity_type_tags.json'));i=json.load(open('kubejs/exported/tags/item_tags.json'));want=[(k,len(v)) for d in (b,i) for k,v in d.items() if k.startswith(('creativeengineering:earth_fill/','creativeengineering:ground_match/')) or k=='creativeengineering:worldgen/grass_like_soils'];want+=[(k,len(v)) for k,v in e.items() if k.endswith('bubble_column_immune')];[print(k,n) for k,n in sorted(want)];empty=[k for k,n in want if n==0];print('empty:',empty);import sys;sys.exit(1 if empty or not want else 0)"
look every listed tag has members; the bubble_column_immune entity tag present

